		{"id":"enum-snmp","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/snmp enum|SNMP]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":-665,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"enum-dns","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/DNS enum|DNS]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":-465,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"enum-web","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Web enum|Web]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":-565,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"choose","type":"text","text":"## Identify OS and attack surface\n\nMap every port to a service, version, hostname, unauthenticated exposure, credentials, and next action.","collapsed":true,"x":1320,"y":-335,"width":480,"height":150,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-rdp","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/RDP enum|RDP]]","collapsed":false,"x":840,"y":-885,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"enum-database","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Database enum|MySQL / MSSQL / PostgreSQL]]","collapsed":false,"x":840,"y":-785,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"enum-ports","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Ports-Actions|Ports → Actions]]","x":-400,"y":-340,"width":180,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-nmap","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/nmap|Nmap workflow]]","x":-1600,"y":-340,"width":180,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-plan","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Plan|Enumeration Plan]]","x":-1900,"y":-340,"width":220,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-heading","type":"text","text":"## Enumeration","x":-2200,"y":-340,"width":180,"height":80,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# OSCP Standalone Box Methodology\n\n**Enumerate → foothold → stabilize/transfer → escalate → proof**\n\nRecord credentials, usernames, ports, failed attempts, and evidence as you work.","x":-620,"y":-1240,"width":800,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"enum-additional","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/Additional services enum|VNC / Redis / Management]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":135,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"enum-ftp","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/FTP enum|FTP]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":235,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"enum-version-scan","type":"text","text":"## 3. Version + default scripts\n\nOnly discovered ports","x":-780,"y":-350,"width":220,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"enum-target-udp","type":"text","text":"## 2. Targeted UDP\n\nTop ports + clues","x":-1080,"y":-350,"width":200,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"enum-full-tcp","type":"text","text":"## 1. Full TCP scan\n\nAll 65,535 ports","x":-1360,"y":-350,"width":200,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ft-intro","type":"text","text":"[[File Transfer/Intro|File Transfer — Overview]]","x":3440,"y":3100,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ft-decision","type":"text","text":"## Select the source and destination","x":3440,"y":3300,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"pa-live","type":"text","text":"# Live login service\n\nConfirm the protocol, username format, failure response, authorization, and lockout policy.","x":3240,"y":970,"width":500,"height":130,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"pa-online","type":"text","text":"[[Definitions/Password attacks/Online Brute Force|Online Brute Force & Password Spraying]]\n\nOne user + wordlist → targeted brute force\nMany users + one password → controlled spray","x":3240,"y":1180,"width":500,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"pa-ntlm","type":"text","text":"# NTLM authentication path\n\n[[Definitions/Password attacks/NTLM Capture & Relay|NTLM Capture & Relay]]","x":3820,"y":970,"width":540,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-signing","type":"text","text":"## Check before relay\n\nGenerate a relay list. Relay only to hosts where SMB signing is not required. Captured NetNTLM is not an NTLM password hash.","x":3820,"y":1400,"width":540,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-result","type":"text","text":"# Credential or access obtained\n\nMap it to a user, host, service, and privilege level. Validate carefully, check permitted reuse, and preserve a clean evidence trail.","x":3040,"y":1720,"width":960,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"pa-throttle","type":"text","text":"## Control authentication noise\n\nThrottle requests and stop on lockouts or unexpected impact. Prefer low-volume validation over indiscriminate guessing.","x":3240,"y":1420,"width":500,"height":150,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-reset","type":"text","text":"## If the path fails\n\nRecheck hash type and formatting, usernames/domains, service responses, lockout policy, SMB signing, and whether captured material is crackable or relayable.","x":3040,"y":1990,"width":960,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ft-windows-linux","type":"text","text":"[[File Transfer/Windows → Linux (Exfil)|Windows → Linux Exfiltration Methods]]","x":4100,"y":3640,"width":440,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-capture","type":"text","text":"## Capture or crack\n\nRun Responder on the correct interface. Save the NetNTLM challenge-response and crack it offline with mode `5600`.","x":3820,"y":1170,"width":540,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-validate","type":"text","text":"## 5. Validate safely\n\nSet the exact target and callback values, prefer a non-destructive check, capture evidence, and stop if behavior differs from expectations.","x":1130,"y":3560,"width":500,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ft-linux-linux","type":"text","text":"[[File Transfer/Linux → Linux|Linux → Linux Transfer Methods]]","x":2760,"y":3640,"width":440,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"chain-b","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain B|Chain B — Anonymous SMB]]\nGuest share → exposed credentials → SSH/WinRM → platform-specific escalation","x":1450,"y":980,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"chain-h","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain H|Chain H — SNMP disclosure]]\nSNMP data → username → controlled spray → SSH/WinRM → local escalation","x":1450,"y":1130,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"chain-i","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain I|Chain I — Predictable password]]\nUsername disclosure → username-derived password → login → local escalation","x":1450,"y":1280,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"attack-nonweb","type":"text","text":"# Non-web / service / credential paths\n\nUse SMB, SNMP, FTP, SMTP, and credential evidence to recover usernames/passwords or obtain direct authenticated access.","x":1290,"y":760,"width":670,"height":150,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"enum-smb","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/SMB enum|SMB]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":-365,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"enum-ssh","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/SSH enum|SSH]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":-275,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pa-title","type":"text","text":"# Password attacks\n\n[[Definitions/Password attacks/Intro|Concepts and attack selection]]\n\nIdentify the credential material first, then choose the least noisy effective path.","x":2660,"y":470,"width":720,"height":170,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"pa-start","type":"text","text":"## What do you have?\n\nA stolen hash, a live login service, or an opportunity to capture/relay NTLM authentication?","x":2660,"y":720,"width":720,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"pa-hash","type":"text","text":"# Hash obtained\n\nPreserve the original and identify its type before cracking.","x":2660,"y":970,"width":500,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pa-crack","type":"text","text":"## Crack offline\n\n`hashcat -m <MODE> hashes.txt rockyou.txt`\n\nFast, silent, and no account lockouts. Add targeted rules only when evidence supports them.","x":2660,"y":1400,"width":500,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"pa-modes","type":"text","text":"[[Definitions/Password attacks/Hash Mode Reference|Hashcat Mode Reference]]\n\nNTLM `1000` · NetNTLMv2 `5600` · Kerberoast `13100` · AS-REP `18200` · SHA512crypt `1800`","x":2660,"y":1170,"width":500,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ft-title","type":"text","text":"# File Transfer\n\nChoose the direction of transfer, then open the corresponding note.","x":3390,"y":2860,"width":520,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ft-linux-windows","type":"text","text":"[[File Transfer/Linux → Windows|Linux → Windows Transfer Methods]]","x":3430,"y":3640,"width":440,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"enum-smtp","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/SMTP enum|SMTP]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":-185,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"enum-winrm","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/WinRM enum|WinRM]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":15,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"enum-rpc-nfs","type":"text","text":"[[Enumeration-stand-alone/RPC-NFS enum|RPC / NFS]]","collapsed":true,"x":840,"y":-85,"width":230,"height":70,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sqli","type":"text","text":"[[Blind SQLi — Time-Based|Blind SQLi — Time-Based]]","x":-3100,"y":960,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"linux-plan","type":"text","text":"[[Plan-standalone-linux|Linux Standalone Plan]]","x":-2890,"y":560,"width":360,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"linux-commands","type":"text","text":"[[Commands|Linux PrivEsc Commands]]","x":-3080,"y":1700,"width":460,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"chain-c","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain C|Chain C — LFI to SSH]]\nLFI → private key disclosure → SSH → unsafe `sudo` rule → root","x":120,"y":1130,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"chain-g","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain G|Chain G — FTP/webroot overlap]]\nAnonymous FTP write → executable web file → `www-data` shell → local escalation","x":960,"y":1510,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"linux-proof","type":"text","text":"## 3. Root and proof\n\nVerify identity and hostname, capture the required proof, and preserve a clean command trail for reporting.","x":-2760,"y":2660,"width":720,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"attack-hybrid","type":"text","text":"### Hybrid path\nChain G starts with FTP but becomes code execution only when the writable FTP location overlaps an executable webroot.","x":880,"y":1350,"width":520,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"shell","type":"text","text":"## [[Shell & upgrade/Intro|Shell handling & upgrade]]\n\nAfter execution/access is obtained: stabilize the session when needed, confirm identity/context, and prepare for local enumeration.","collapsed":false,"x":780,"y":2100,"width":540,"height":110,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"upload","type":"text","text":"[[File Upload Bypass|File Upload Bypass]]","x":-3100,"y":1110,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"udf","type":"text","text":"[[MySQL UDF RCE (root creds + FILE priv)|MySQL UDF RCE]]","x":-3100,"y":1260,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"linux-foothold","type":"text","text":"## 2. Foothold obtained\n\nConfirm `whoami`, stabilize the shell, inventory credentials/configuration, and transfer tools if needed.","x":-3370,"y":1460,"width":720,"height":130,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"lfi","type":"text","text":"[[LFI-Local File Inclusion|LFI — Local File Inclusion]]","x":-3640,"y":1260,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"chain-d","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain D|Chain D — Unsafe upload]]\nDefault login → upload bypass → web shell → writable root cron script","x":120,"y":1280,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"chain-f","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain F|Chain F — Exposed Git history]]\nPublic `.git` → historical secret → SSH → unsafe `sudo` rule → root","x":540,"y":1130,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"chain-j","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain J|Chain J — SQLi to OS shell]]\nSQL injection → DB execution feature → service-account shell → local escalation","x":540,"y":1280,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"foothold-decision","type":"text","text":"## Initial foothold obtained?\n\n**Yes:** usable code execution, shell, SSH, WinRM, RDP, or another authenticated session.\n\n**No:** return to enumeration and test the next evidence-backed path.","x":650,"y":1760,"width":800,"height":180,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"win-token","type":"text","text":"[[Token Priviledge|Windows Token Privileges]]","x":-820,"y":1080,"width":520,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"win-creds","type":"text","text":"[[Dump Credentials (Windows Post-Exploitation)|Dump Windows Credentials]]","x":-1160,"y":1320,"width":620,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"win-proof","type":"text","text":"## SYSTEM/Administrator and proof\n\nVerify the security context and hostname, capture the required proof, and document the successful chain.","x":-1230,"y":1550,"width":720,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"linux-tree","type":"text","text":"[[Decision Tree|Linux PrivEsc Decision Tree]]","x":-2400,"y":1700,"width":460,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cmdi","type":"text","text":"[[Command Injection|Command Injection]]","x":-2560,"y":960,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"git","type":"text","text":"[[git Exposed → Credential Chain|.git Exposed → Credential Chain]]","x":-2560,"y":1110,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ssti","type":"text","text":"[[SSTI — Server-Side Template Injection|SSTI — Server-Side Template Injection]]","x":-2560,"y":1260,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"exif","type":"text","text":"[[Exiftool — Metadata → Usernames|ExifTool — Metadata → Usernames]]","x":-3640,"y":1110,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"chain-a","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain A|Chain A — Web CVE]]\nVersion fingerprint → RCE → config credentials → SSH reuse → `sudo` → root","x":120,"y":980,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"chains","type":"text","text":"## [[Plan-Summary-Attacks|Attack-chain selection]]\n\nUse evidence from service enumeration to choose the lowest-noise path to **code execution** or **valid credentials**. Do not force a chain when the evidence does not fit.","x":120,"y":520,"width":620,"height":170,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"win-initial","type":"text","text":"[[Initial Access|Windows Initial Access]]","x":-720,"y":610,"width":500,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"win-foothold","type":"text","text":"## Foothold obtained\n\nConfirm `whoami`, `hostname`, integrity level, groups, architecture, and available tooling before choosing a path.","x":-1230,"y":830,"width":720,"height":130,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"win-header","type":"text","text":"# Windows path\n\nEnumerate exposed services, gain execution, then check privileges, service/configuration weaknesses, stored credentials, and patch level.","x":-1500,"y":590,"width":650,"height":150,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"win-pe-plan","type":"text","text":"[[StandAloneBoxes/Standalone Win Box Methodology/Priviledge Escalation/Plan|Windows Privilege Escalation Plan]]","x":-1500,"y":1080,"width":520,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"linux-header","type":"text","text":"# Linux path\n\nWeb enumeration is often the entry point. Turn a supported finding into execution, obtain a stable shell, then enumerate locally for root.","x":-3640,"y":540,"width":620,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"chain-e","type":"text","text":"### [[Chain E|Chain E — PHP source disclosure]]\nLFI/filter → DB credentials → SQL file write → web shell → local escalation","x":540,"y":980,"width":350,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"linux-pe-plan","type":"text","text":"[[StandAloneBoxes/Standalone Linux Box Methodology/Linux Privilege Escalation/plan|Linux Privilege Escalation Plan]]","x":-4570,"y":1700,"width":460,"height":100,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"attack-web","type":"text","text":"# Web / application paths\n\nUse HTTP(S) findings such as version fingerprints, LFI, unsafe upload, SQL injection, or exposed `.git` to reach execution or recover credentials.","x":120,"y":760,"width":770,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"linux-vs-windows","type":"text","text":"#### Linux vs Windows — the two worlds\n\nOSCP boxes are either Linux or Windows, and the \"god user\" is named differently on each. Everything else — the loop — stays the same.\n\n| | **Linux** | **Windows** |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Top admin user** | `root` | `SYSTEM` / Administrator |\n| **You'll often start via** | a web app on port 80 | SMB (445), RDP, or AD creds |\n| **Where passwords hide** | `/etc/shadow`, config files | SAM, LSASS memory, AD database |\n| **Privilege-escalation hunt** | sudo, SUID, cron | tokens, services, AD misconfigs |","x":-3500,"y":-40,"width":1100,"height":430,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"archive","type":"text","text":"[[Archive - ZIP Cracking|Archive / ZIP Cracking]]","x":-3640,"y":960,"width":460,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"web-hub","type":"text","text":"## 1. Web foothold techniques\n\nTest what the discovered technology and behavior support.","x":-3640,"y":770,"width":430,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-ad-head","type":"text","text":"# Active Directory CVEs\n\nConfirm the domain controller, patch state, authentication level, and ADCS availability before selecting a chain.","x":800,"y":4200,"width":840,"height":150,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-ad-note","type":"text","text":"[[ZeroLogon and noPac|ZeroLogon, noPac, and Certifried notes]]","x":800,"y":4420,"width":840,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-zerologon","type":"text","text":"## ZeroLogon — CVE-2020-1472\n\nUnpatched Netlogon secure channel weakness on a domain controller → domain compromise without credentials. Treat as high impact and verify patch state carefully.","x":800,"y":4610,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-nopac","type":"text","text":"## noPac — CVE-2021-42278 + CVE-2021-42287\n\nsAMAccountName spoofing chain → Domain Admin from a low-privileged domain user when prerequisites and missing patches align.","x":800,"y":4890,"width":840,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-certifried","type":"text","text":"## Certifried — CVE-2022-26923\n\nADCS plus machine-account identity spoofing → authenticate as a domain controller and escalate. Requires an applicable CA/template and account-control conditions.","x":800,"y":5160,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cve-ad-links","type":"text","text":"## Detailed playbooks\n\n[[Active Directory/Attack-Phases/Phase-2-3/ZeroLogon — Unauthenticated Domain Admin (CVE-2020-1472)|ZeroLogon playbook]]\n\n[[Active Directory/Attack-Phases/Phase-2-3/noPac- SamAccountName Spoofing — Low-Priv User to DA (CVE-2021-42278 + CVE-2021-42287)|noPac playbook]]\n\n[[Active Directory/Attack-Phases/Phase-2-3/ADCS — Active Directory Certificate Services|ADCS playbook]]","x":800,"y":5440,"width":840,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-intro","type":"text","text":"[[Definitions/Common CVEs & Exploits/Intro|Start here: CVE safety and selection]]","x":-1640,"y":3600,"width":420,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-local-head","type":"text","text":"# Local root candidates\n\nConsider these after obtaining a shell and checking the installed package/kernel versions and exploit prerequisites.","x":-420,"y":4200,"width":840,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-local-userland","type":"text","text":"## Userland / setuid paths\n\n- **CVE-2021-3156 Baron Samedit** — sudo before 1.9.5p2 → local root\n- **CVE-2021-4034 PwnKit** — vulnerable pkexec/polkit → local root\n- **CVE-2023-4911 Looney Tunables** — vulnerable glibc `ld.so` on affected distributions → local root","x":-420,"y":4440,"width":840,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-local-kernel","type":"text","text":"## Kernel paths\n\n- **CVE-2022-0847 Dirty Pipe** — affected Linux kernels in the 5.8–5.16.11 range → local root\n- **CVE-2016-5195 Dirty COW** — affected older kernels → local root\n\nKernel exploits can destabilize a host; confirm the exact build and constraints first.","x":-420,"y":4820,"width":840,"height":300,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-local-enum","type":"text","text":"## Evidence to collect\n\n`uname -a` · `/etc/os-release` · package versions · glibc version · architecture · mount options · available compiler/tooling","x":-420,"y":5220,"width":840,"height":170,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-local-check","type":"text","text":"## Prefer simpler paths first\n\nCheck sudo rights, SUID/capabilities, writable services/scripts, credentials, cron/systemd jobs, and exposed local services before choosing a risky kernel exploit.","x":-420,"y":5490,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cve-reference","type":"text","text":"[[CVEs|Open the complete CVE shortlist]]","x":-410,"y":5920,"width":820,"height":110,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-result","type":"text","text":"# Record the outcome\n\nDocument the detected version, supporting evidence, exploit source, modifications, command used, returned security context, and cleanup. If the match is uncertain, return to enumeration.","x":-500,"y":6140,"width":1000,"height":190,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"reset","type":"text","text":"## If progress stalls\n\nReturn to enumeration. Recheck UDP, virtual hosts, authenticated features, files/metadata, credential reuse, local-only services, and exact versions. Avoid guessing exploits without evidence.","x":-450,"y":2940,"width":900,"height":170,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cve-title","type":"text","text":"# Common CVEs & Exploits\n\n**Fingerprint → match exact version → inspect exploit → validate safely → document result**\n\nUse this map only against systems you are authorized to test.","x":-900,"y":3280,"width":840,"height":190,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cve-verify","type":"text","text":"## 3. Verify the candidate\n\nConfirm affected versions, prerequisites, authentication, exploit reliability, and required edits. Read the code before running it.","x":-10,"y":3560,"width":480,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-fingerprint","type":"text","text":"## 1. Fingerprint precisely\n\nRecord product, exact version/build, OS and architecture, exposed feature, and reachable port.","x":-1120,"y":3570,"width":440,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-head","type":"text","text":"# Remote exploitation\n\nUse only when enumeration proves the exposed product and vulnerable version or configuration.","x":-1640,"y":4200,"width":840,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-win","type":"text","text":"## Windows network services\n\n- **MS17-010 EternalBlue** — Windows 7 / Server 2008 R2, SMBv1 → SYSTEM\n- **CVE-2019-0708 BlueKeep** — Windows 7 / Server 2008, RDP → RCE/SYSTEM\n- **CVE-2020-0796 SMBGhost** — SMBv3 compression, Windows 10 / Server 2019 → RCE/SYSTEM\n- **CVE-2021-1675 PrintNightmare** — Windows print spooler → SYSTEM/RCE","x":-1640,"y":4420,"width":840,"height":300,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-web","type":"text","text":"## Web and application servers\n\n- **CVE-2021-41773** — Apache 2.4.49 path traversal → RCE\n- **CVE-2021-44228 Log4Shell** — Log4j 2.x → RCE\n- **CVE-2022-26134** — Confluence OGNL injection → RCE\n- **CVE-2021-22205** — GitLab ExifTool avatar upload → RCE","x":-1640,"y":4800,"width":840,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-enterprise","type":"text","text":"## Enterprise applications\n\n- **ProxyShell** — CVE-2021-34473 / 34523 / 31207, Exchange → RCE/SYSTEM\n- **ProxyLogon** — CVE-2021-26855, Exchange → pre-auth RCE\n- **CVE-2023-22515 / 22518** — Confluence access-control failure → admin creation / RCE\n- **CVE-2023-38408** — OpenSSH < 9.3p2 with forwarded ssh-agent → RCE","x":-1640,"y":5180,"width":840,"height":330,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"cve-remote-check","type":"text","text":"## Gate before execution\n\nExact build confirmed? Required service/feature enabled? Network path reachable? Exploit source reviewed? Crash or cleanup risk understood?","x":-1640,"y":5560,"width":840,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"cve-searchsploit","type":"text","text":"[[Searchsploit|2. Searchsploit commands]]\n\nSearch locally, open the source, then copy only the candidate you intend to inspect.","x":-570,"y":3570,"width":450,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cve-classify","type":"text","text":"## 4. Choose the matching path\n\nIs this remote code execution, local privilege escalation, or an Active Directory escalation?","x":580,"y":3575,"width":450,"height":150,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"attack-reset","type":"text","text":"### No foothold yet\nRe-check ports/UDP, virtual hosts, shares/files, usernames, credential reuse, authenticated features, and exact versions.","x":1600,"y":1900,"width":390,"height":140,"color":"2"}
	],
